@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# MarketScanner — environment variables
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Copy to `.env`, fill in the secrets, and either source it before launching
+# (`set -a && source .env && set +a`) or wire it into your process manager.
+# Variables marked REQUIRED must be set or the API will refuse to start.
+
+# ── Core process ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+# REQUIRED. The HTTP listen port. Replit typically injects PORT automatically;
+# locally pick something free (5000 is the convention in this repo).
+PORT=5000
+
+# Whether the server emits dev-friendly logs and skips Secure cookies.
+# One of: development, production, test.
+NODE_ENV=development
+
+# Optional. Pino log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal.
+# Default: info in production, debug in development.
+LOG_LEVEL=info
+
+# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+# REQUIRED. Postgres connection string. Drizzle ORM uses this for the kite
+# session table, TradingView alert log, FII/DII flow cache, and the new
+# user_session table (sliding-session auth).
+# Format: postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DBNAME
+DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost:5432/marketscanner
+
+# ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+# REQUIRED. Secret used by cookie-parser to sign the `scanner_session` cookie.
+# Rotate this and every existing session is invalidated. Use a 32-char+ random
+# string; do NOT reuse the APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD value.
+#
+# Generate one with:    openssl rand -hex 32
+SESSION_SECRET=
+
+# REQUIRED for use. Single shared password that gates the SPA. The login
+# endpoint compares a submitted password to this in constant time. If unset,
+# the server boots but every login attempt returns 503 (the SPA shows a
+# "login is not configured" hint).
+APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD=
+
+# Optional. Comma-separated list of origins allowed to call /api with
+# credentials. Defaults to the empty list, meaning "same-origin only" (which
+# is what you want for the Replit deployment). Set "*" to opt back into the
+# legacy "reflect any origin" behaviour for local dev only.
+# Example: CORS_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com,https://staging.example.com
+CORS_ORIGINS=
+
+# ── Kite Connect (Zerodha live tick feed) ────────────────────────────────────
+# Both must be set together; if either is missing, the server still boots and
+# falls back to the Yahoo Finance delayed quote provider.
+
+# Optional. Kite Connect API key from https://developers.kite.trade/
+KITE_API_KEY=
+
+# Optional. Kite Connect API secret. Stored only on the server; the SPA never
+# sees it. Used during the daily callback to exchange request_token for
+# access_token.
+KITE_API_SECRET=
+
+# ── TradingView webhooks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+# Optional. Required only in production. POST /api/webhooks/tradingview rejects
+# every alert without this secret in the request (header X-Webhook-Secret,
+# query ?secret=, or body {"secret":"..."} ).
+# Rotate by changing on the server; existing TV alert configs need to be
+# updated to match.
+TRADINGVIEW_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
