@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@
+# MarketScanner
+
+Live NSE/BSE market scanner with options analytics, F&O OI lab, multi-leg
+strategy builder, news catalysts, and a TradingView webhook ingest. Built on
+an Express 5 / TanStack Query stack, connected to Zerodha Kite for live ticks
+and Yahoo Finance as a fallback for delayed quotes.
+
+This README is the entry point for someone cloning the repo. For the deeper
+architectural notes and the running fix-log, see [`replit.md`](./replit.md).
+
+> **Status (April 2026):** internal/private workspace. Single-tenant — one
+> shared `APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD` gates the entire SPA. Sliding sessions, CSRF
+> tokens, and a CORS allowlist are wired up; multi-user with per-user audit
+> is not yet implemented.
+
+---
+
+## Repository layout
+
+```
+artifacts/
+  api-server/       Express 5 backend — Pino logging, Drizzle ORM,
+                    Black-Scholes options pricing, scoring engine, OI Lab,
+                    TradingView webhook ingest. Strict TS, ~13.6k LOC.
+  scanner/          React 19 SPA — Vite + TanStack Query + Tailwind. ~30
+                    pages including dashboard, full-NSE scan, deep-scan,
+                    options strategies, OI Lab.
+
+lib/
+  api-spec/         OpenAPI 3.1 schema (single source of truth for every
+                    `/api/*` endpoint — 55 paths).
+  api-zod/          Zod schemas auto-generated from openapi.yaml.
+  api-client-react/ Orval-generated TanStack Query hooks + customFetch
+                    helper. The SPA's only HTTP entry point.
+  db/               Drizzle schema + Postgres pool. Tables: kite_session,
+                    tv_alerts, inst_flows, user_session.
+
+scripts/            One-off operational scripts (NSE bhavcopy fetch, etc.).
+```
+
+The codebase is a pnpm-workspace monorepo. The root `package.json`'s
+`preinstall` script enforces pnpm — `npm install` and `yarn` are rejected.
+
+---
+
+## Quick start
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+* **Node.js ≥ 20** (the api-server uses `node --enable-source-maps` and
+  `Intl.DateTimeFormat` for IST handling).
+* **pnpm ≥ 9** (`corepack enable && corepack prepare pnpm@latest --activate`).
+* **PostgreSQL ≥ 14** for the session/Kite token tables. SQLite is *not*
+  supported — Drizzle is configured against `drizzle-orm/node-postgres`.
+* **(Optional) Kite Connect developer account** if you want live ticks.
+
+### Setup
+
+```bash
+git clone <this repo>
+cd marketscanner
+pnpm install                          # enforces pnpm; nothing else works
+cp .env.example .env
+# edit .env: set DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD
+pnpm -F @workspace/db db:push         # creates the 4 tables in Postgres
+pnpm -F @workspace/api-server dev     # API on :5000 by default
+pnpm -F @workspace/scanner dev        # SPA on :5173
+```
+
+Open `http://localhost:5173`. The login screen prompts for the
+`APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD` you set in `.env`.
+
+### Run the test suite
+
+```bash
+pnpm -F @workspace/api-server test               # 166 unit tests
+pnpm -F @workspace/api-server test:coverage      # coverage report → ./coverage
+pnpm -F @workspace/api-client-react test         # customFetch tests
+```
+
+The api-server tests are pure — no Postgres or Kite required. The
+`@workspace/db` mock keeps everything in-process. Coverage focuses on the
+math-heavy modules (`blackScholes`, `scoring`, `optionStrategies`,
+`indicators`, `oiLab`, `auth`, `kiteAuth`).
+
+### Type-check the whole monorepo
+
+```bash
+pnpm typecheck      # exits non-zero if any workspace fails
+```
+
+---
+
+## Operational topics
+
+### Authentication
+
+* **One shared password** (`APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD`) authorises every request.
+* On successful login the server creates a row in `user_session` and sets a
+  signed httpOnly cookie carrying an opaque 64-char ID.
+* Every authenticated request looks up the row and **slides the expiry
+  forward** (throttled to one DB write per minute). Active users are never
+  logged out at the 30-day boundary.
+* `POST /api/auth/logout` deletes the row, so a stolen cookie can be revoked
+  instantly.
+* State-changing endpoints (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) require an
+  `X-CSRF-Token` header that matches the per-session token returned by
+  `GET /api/auth/status`. The token is also returned in `POST /api/auth/login`'s
+  response.
+* Expired session rows are reaped on boot and once an hour after.
+
+### CORS
+
+Set `CORS_ORIGINS` to a CSV of allowed origins (default: same-origin only).
+Use `*` for "reflect any origin" in development. The previous behaviour
+(`origin: true`) is gone — that pattern is the Mozilla-flagged broad-CORS
+anti-pattern when paired with `credentials: true`.
+
+### Kite Connect
+
+* The Kite access token expires at ~06:00 IST every morning.
+* `GET /api/kite/login-url` returns the Zerodha OAuth URL.
+* After the user logs in on Zerodha, the redirect lands on
+  `/api/kite/callback?request_token=...`, which exchanges it for an
+  access token and persists the row in `kite_session`.
+* `next6amIST` (in `kiteAuth.ts`) computes the exact moment of expiry using
+  `Intl.DateTimeFormat('Asia/Kolkata')` — DST-safe and unit-tested.
+* If Kite is not configured, every Kite-aware feature degrades to Yahoo:
+  delayed quotes work but tick-level OI deltas don't.
+
+### Rate limits
+
+| Path                           | Window  | Limit        | Notes                                |
+| ------------------------------ | ------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------ |
+| `/api/auth/login`              | 15 min  | 5 / IP       | Successful logins are not counted    |
+| `/api/webhooks/*`              | 1 min   | 60 / IP      | TradingView burst-friendly           |
+| `/api/*` (everything else)     | 1 min   | 300 / IP     | Default per-IP cap                   |
+
+### TradingView webhooks
+
+`POST /api/webhooks/tradingview` is the only public state-changing endpoint.
+In production it requires `TRADINGVIEW_WEBHOOK_SECRET` to be supplied via:
+
+* `?secret=...` querystring, or
+* `X-Webhook-Secret` header, or
+* `secret` field in the JSON body.
+
+`GET /api/webhooks/tradingview` (auth required) lists recent alerts;
+`DELETE /api/webhooks/tradingview` clears them (also requires the secret).
+
+### Logs and observability
+
+Pino structured JSON to stdout. `pino-pretty` is bundled — pipe through it in
+development:
+
+```bash
+pnpm -F @workspace/api-server dev | pnpm exec pino-pretty
+```
+
+There is currently **no** `/metrics` endpoint, error reporter, or trace
+exporter. See the open issues list at the bottom of this file.
+
+---
+
+## API spec
+
+The single source of truth is [`lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml`](./lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml).
+Every `/api/*` endpoint is documented (55 paths, 86 schemas). The orval
+config in `lib/api-client-react/orval.config.ts` regenerates the typed
+TanStack Query hooks from this file:
+
+```bash
+pnpm -F @workspace/api-client-react gen
+```
+
+If you add a route in `artifacts/api-server`, **also** update the OpenAPI
+spec in the same change. The TypeScript build will succeed regardless, but
+the SPA loses type safety for the new endpoint.
+
+The OpenAPI document is validated on every PR (CI step `validate-openapi`).
+You can run it locally:
+
+```bash
+pip install --user openapi-spec-validator
+python3 -c 'from openapi_spec_validator import validate; import yaml; validate(yaml.safe_load(open("lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml")))'
+```
+
+---
+
+## Architecture highlights
+
+### Scoring engine (`artifacts/api-server/src/lib/scoring.ts`)
+
+* 13 weighted rules produce a score in `[-100, +100]`.
+* Cutoffs: `≥ 50` STRONG_BUY, `≥ 22` BUY, `≥ -22` NEUTRAL, `≥ -50` SELL,
+  else STRONG_SELL.
+* When an indicator (ADX, volume ratio, delivery %) isn't computed for a
+  symbol, the corresponding rule is **skipped** — it does not contribute
+  fake "neutral" weight that biases the score toward zero.
+* The `confidence` field is the *alignment* of evidence (what fraction of
+  weighted reasons agree with the final direction), not a probability of
+  trade success. A back-test harness for predictive validity is on the
+  roadmap.
+* Stop-loss is capped at `price × 0.999` for BUYs (mirror for SELLs) so a
+  fast breakdown that pushes price below the lagging 20-day support can
+  never invert the trade.
+
+### Options pricing (`artifacts/api-server/src/lib/blackScholes.ts`)
+
+* Standard Black-Scholes-Merton with continuous dividend yield `q`.
+* Newton-Raphson IV solver with bisection fallback over `σ ∈ [0.01, 5.0]`.
+* `yearsToExpiry` anchors at the 15:30 IST settlement instant (10:00 UTC)
+  and floors at 1 hour to keep Greeks finite at expiry.
+
+### OI Lab (`artifacts/api-server/src/lib/oiLab.ts`)
+
+* `computeOiInsights` produces a per-strike OI bar chart, max-pain, PCR,
+  ATM IV, sentiment band, and a 1-line interpretation.
+* `fetchOiHeatmap` uses the Kite NFO instruments dump + a session OI baseline
+  (mid-of-day-high-and-low) to classify every F&O equity into LONG_BUILDUP,
+  SHORT_BUILDUP, SHORT_COVERING, LONG_UNWINDING, or NEUTRAL.
+* The intraday `tracker` polls every 1–60 minutes and persists snapshots to
+  disk so a server restart mid-day keeps the chart history.
+* Max-pain tie-breaker prefers the strike closest to spot.
+
+### Strategy builder (`artifacts/api-server/src/lib/optionStrategies.ts`)
+
+* 13 strategy templates: long call/put, straddles, strangles, call/put
+  spreads, iron condor, iron butterfly, covered call.
+* Each strategy returns a fully-computed payoff curve, breakevens, signed
+  max P/L, net Greeks, probability-of-profit, and a recommendation flag.
+* **Cash-settled indices** (NIFTY, BANKNIFTY, FINNIFTY, MIDCPNIFTY,
+  NIFTYNXT50, SENSEX, BANKEX) skip Covered Call instead of synthesising a
+  fake "long stock" leg — the previous behaviour produced absurd Max Loss
+  values like ₹15.43 lakh on NIFTY. Tested.
+
+---
+
+## Known gaps / roadmap
+
+These are tracked in the code review's "What is missing / requires fix"
+sections. The biggest items still open:
+
+* `/metrics` (Prometheus) endpoint and a metrics counter for: scans completed,
+  Yahoo retries, Kite reconnects, IV-solve failures, RSS feed failures.
+* Sentry-style error reporter for the SPA (currently silent breadcrumbs).
+* Backtest harness for the scoring engine (predict forward returns; calibrate
+  the rule weights and signal cutoffs against actual hit-rates).
+* SSE / WebSocket push from the Kite feed to the SPA dashboard so the
+  ticker doesn't poll every 30s.
+* Versioned Drizzle migrations (currently `db:push` workflow — fine for
+  development, dangerous in production).
+* Replace the `1500-row` full-NSE-scan response with a streaming variant
+  for mobile.
+
+---
+
+## Contributing
+
+1. Fork or create a branch.
+2. Make your change. If you add a route, **update `openapi.yaml`** and
+   regenerate the client.
+3. Add or extend a Vitest suite. The bar for math/finance code is "table
+   tests with reference values from a known-correct source" (Hull, QuantLib,
+   pandas-ta, etc.) — see `blackScholes.test.ts` for the pattern.
+4. `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm -F @workspace/api-server test` must both
+   exit zero.
+5. Open a PR. CI runs typecheck, tests, OpenAPI validation, and
+   `pnpm audit --audit-level=high`.
+
+---
+
